# api-server test rig. Copy to .env — .env is gitignored, this file is not, so keep
# real secrets OUT of it.
#
# The DB tests are gated twice on purpose: they only run when DATABASE_URL is set,
# AND createE2EPool() hard-refuses any host/database outside the dev allow-list
# (helium / heliumdb on localhost). That is an opt-in allow-list, not a deny-list,
# so the production DB can never be reached even by accident. Never set
# KFI_E2E_ALLOW_DB in production.
#
# Bootstrap the local DB once:
#   createdb -h 127.0.0.1 heliumdb
#   cd lib/db && pnpm exec drizzle-kit push --force --config ./drizzle.config.ts
# (`pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push` runs pre-migrate first, which expects an
#  EXISTING schema and fails on an empty database — push directly to bootstrap.)
DATABASE_URL=postgres://<you>@127.0.0.1:5432/heliumdb
KFI_E2E_ALLOW_DB=1
